---An Instance is a computing unit that an end customer can connect to. It's the main unit of computing resources in AlloyDB.
---@class gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.Instance
---@field pscInstanceInfo? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.PscInstanceInfo Output only. Information about the Private Service Connect (PSC) for the instance.
---@field writableNode? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.Node Output only. This is set for the read-write VM of the PRIMARY instance only.
---@field observabilityConfig? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.ObservabilityInstanceConfig Configuration for observability.
---@field name? string Output only. The name of the instance resource with the format: * projects/{project}/locations/{region}/clusters/{cluster_id}/instances/{instance_id} where the cluster and instance ID segments should satisfy the regex expression `[a-z]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?`, e.g. 1-63 characters of lowercase letters, numbers, and dashes, starting with a letter, and ending with a letter or number. For more details see https://google.aip.dev/122. The prefix of the instance resource name is the name of the parent resource: * projects/{project}/locations/{region}/clusters/{cluster_id}
---@field annotations? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.StringMap Annotations to allow client tools to store small amount of arbitrary data. This is distinct from labels. https://google.aip.dev/128
---@field dataApiAccess? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.InstanceDataApiAccessEnum Optional. Controls whether the Data API is enabled for this instance. When enabled, this allows authorized users to connect to the instance from the public internet using the `executeSql` API, even for private IP instances. If this is not specified, the data API is enabled by default for Google internal services like AlloyDB Studio. Disable it explicitly to disallow Google internal services as well.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.StringMap Labels as key value pairs
---@field maintenanceVersionName? string Output only. Maintenance version of the instance, for example: POSTGRES_15.2025_07_15.04_00. Output only. Update this field via the parent cluster's maintenance_version field(s).
---@field etag? string For Resource freshness validation (https://google.aip.dev/154)
---@field queryInsightsInfo? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.QueryInsightsInstanceInfo Output only. Instance level Query Insights information, which is read-only and available in the output only. Contains the effective query insights settings for this instance, by merging customer's provided `QueryInsightsInstanceConfig` with the Query Insights defaults.
---@field gcaConfig? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.GCAInstanceConfig Output only. Configuration parameters related to Gemini Cloud Assist.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Update time stamp
---@field instanceType? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.InstanceInstanceTypeEnum Required. The type of the instance. Specified at creation time.
---@field activationPolicy? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.InstanceActivationPolicyEnum Optional. Specifies whether an instance needs to spin up. Once the instance is active, the activation policy can be updated to the `NEVER` to stop the instance. Likewise, the activation policy can be updated to `ALWAYS` to start the instance. There are restrictions around when an instance can/cannot be activated (for example, a read pool instance should be stopped before stopping primary etc.). Please refer to the API documentation for more details.
---@field readPoolConfig? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.ReadPoolConfig Read pool instance configuration. This is required if the value of instanceType is READ_POOL.
---@field gceZone? string The Compute Engine zone that the instance should serve from, per https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/regions-zones This can ONLY be specified for ZONAL instances. If present for a REGIONAL instance, an error will be thrown. If this is absent for a ZONAL instance, instance is created in a random zone with available capacity.
---@field deleteTime? string Output only. Delete time stamp
---@field outboundPublicIpAddresses? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.StringList Output only. All outbound public IP addresses configured for the instance.
---@field geminiConfig? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.GeminiInstanceConfig Optional. Deprecated and unused. This field will be removed in the near future.
---@field connectionPoolConfig? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.ConnectionPoolConfig Optional. The configuration for Managed Connection Pool (MCP).
---@field displayName? string User-settable and human-readable display name for the Instance.
---@field uid? string Output only. The system-generated UID of the resource. The UID is assigned when the resource is created, and it is retained until it is deleted.
---@field publicIpAddress? string Output only. The public IP address for the Instance. This is available ONLY when `enable_public_ip` is set or when you have upgraded from an Express Instance that has public DNS enabled. This field is not available for Express Instances. This is the connection endpoint for an end-user application.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field databaseFlags? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.StringMap Database flags. Set at the instance level. They are copied from the primary instance on secondary instance creation. Flags that have restrictions default to the value at primary instance on read instances during creation. Read instances can set new flags or override existing flags that are relevant for reads, for example, for enabling columnar cache on a read instance. Flags set on read instance might or might not be present on the primary instance. This is a list of "key": "value" pairs. "key": The name of the flag. These flags are passed at instance setup time, so include both server options and system variables for Postgres. Flags are specified with underscores, not hyphens. "value": The value of the flag. Booleans are set to **on** for true and **off** for false. This field must be omitted if the flag doesn't take a value.
---@field reconciling? boolean Output only. Reconciling (https://google.aip.dev/128#reconciliation). Set to true if the current state of Instance does not match the user's intended state, and the service is actively updating the resource to reconcile them. This can happen due to user-triggered updates or system actions like failover or maintenance.
---@field ipAddress? string Output only. The IP address for the Instance. This is the connection endpoint for an end-user application.
---@field queryInsightsConfig? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.QueryInsightsInstanceConfig Configuration for query insights.
---@field observabilityInstanceInfo? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.ObservabilityInstanceInfo Output only. Instance level observability information, contains the effective values of observability settings for this instance, by merging customer's provided `ObservabilityInstanceConfig` with the Observability defaults.
---@field networkConfig? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.InstanceNetworkConfig Optional. Instance-level network configuration.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.InstanceStateEnum Output only. The current serving state of the instance.
---@field nodes? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.NodeList Output only. List of available read-only VMs in this instance, including the standby for a PRIMARY instance.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Create time stamp
---@field clientConnectionConfig? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.ClientConnectionConfig Optional. Client connection specific configurations
---@field updatePolicy? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.UpdatePolicy Update policy that will be applied during instance update. This field is not persisted when you update the instance. To use a non-default update policy, you must specify explicitly specify the value in each update request.
---@field availabilityType? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.InstanceAvailabilityTypeEnum Availability type of an Instance. If empty, defaults to REGIONAL for primary instances. For read pools, availability_type is always UNSPECIFIED. Instances in the read pools are evenly distributed across available zones within the region (i.e. read pools with more than one node will have a node in at least two zones).
---@field pscInstanceConfig? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.PscInstanceConfig Optional. The configuration for Private Service Connect (PSC) for the instance.
---@field networkInfo? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.InstanceNetworkInfo Output only. Instance-level network information.
---@field machineConfig? gcp.unstable.alloydb_v1alpha.MachineConfig Configurations for the machines that host the underlying database engine.

